{"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Composing Large Games","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/SplittingAGameAcrossFiles","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContents","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ScoreDeclaring"],"anchor":"Composing-Large-Games"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A content bundle ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") splits a game’s own world across types and packages. A plugin does something else: it packages a reusable "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"system","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" — spellcasting, a wall clock, combat — so a second game can import it. The seven "},{"code":"Gnusto*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" libraries in this repo are all built this way, and so is the "},{"code":"buy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"sell","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" logic you would otherwise hand-copy into every shop game."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin is "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"logic only","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":". It contributes the vocabulary its system needs and the rules that react to it, and owns no rooms, items, or "},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" state; everything it touches is declared by the host game and handed to it as a parameter. A plugin that needs a room of its own is not a plugin."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"A plugin is a `GamePlugin`","anchor":"A-plugin-is-a-GamePlugin"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["extension Intent {","    #verb(\"haggle\", [\"haggle\", \"over\", .directObject])","}","","struct CommercePlugin: GamePlugin {","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] {","        .haggle","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"actions","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" all default to empty, so a plugin declares only what it needs. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#verb"},{"text":" declarations (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") give the plugin ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" its hosts the same typed constants — host rules key on "},{"code":".haggle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" exactly as the plugin’s verbs emit it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note what "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"isn’t","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" declared here. "},{"code":"buy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"sell","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are engine stub verbs (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StubVerbs","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), so the words are already in every game’s vocabulary; a commerce plugin only has to supply the behavior, which it does with the rules below. "},{"code":"haggle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is genuinely the plugin’s own, so it needs the "},{"code":"#verb","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"code":"GnustoMeleeCombat","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" splits the same way: the "},{"code":"attack","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" family is promoted, "},{"code":"stab","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"strike","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are added."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin’s "},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" splice the same way (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var timers: [TimedEvent] { actors.timers }"},{"text":"), and parameterized timer ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"factories"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — methods returning a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TimedEvent","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the host’s own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timers"},{"text":" block — are how a plugin animates the host’s actors on the end-of-turn clock. Timer names are global to the game: prefix yours by convention (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"actors.roam\""},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The host splices verbs and rules","anchor":"The-host-splices-verbs-and-rules"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The host stores the plugin as a plain property and splices its vocabulary into its own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verbs"},{"text":" block. A plain plugin property is neither a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", nor ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"type":"text","text":", so the bootstrap’s reflection walk ignores it — it never becomes an entity and never collides."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":".price","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" below is a "},{"code":"TraitKey<Int>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" declared once ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"extension TraitKey<Int> { static let price = Self(\"price\") }"},{"type":"text","text":") — see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct LampShop: Game {","    let commerce = CommercePlugin()","    @Global var purse = Purse(coins: 10)          \/\/ the HOST owns the wallet","    let lantern = Item { name(\"brass lantern\"); trait(.price, 5) }","","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] { commerce.verbs }    \/\/ splice the vocabulary","    \/\/ rules below","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Parameterized rules over host entities","anchor":"Parameterized-rules-over-host-entities","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin’s rules need the host’s own lantern and purse — things it can’t know about in advance. So rules that touch host state are exposed as "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"parameterized methods","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" returning "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which the host calls with its own declarations. The wallet is handed in as closures that read and adjust the host’s "},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; they run under the live turn, so they see and mutate state exactly as an inline rule would."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension CommercePlugin {","    @RuleBuilder","    func purchase(","        of item: Item,","        balance: @escaping @Sendable () -> Int,","        charge:  @escaping @Sendable (Int) -> Void","    ) -> Rules {","        item.before(.buy) {","            let price = item[.price] ?? 0","            guard balance() >= price else {","                try refuse(\"You can't afford the \\(item.name); it costs \\(price) coins.\")","            }","            charge(price)","            try reply(\"You buy the \\(item.name) for \\(price) coins. You have \\(balance()) left.\")","        }","    }","}","","\/\/ in the host:","var rules: Rules {","    commerce.purchase(of: lantern,","                      balance: { purse.coins },","                      charge:  { purse.coins -= $0 })","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The protocol’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"type":"text","text":" requirement is for self-contained, world-scoped rules that need nothing from the host; anything host-specific goes through a factory method like this."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"A plugin can contribute only vocabulary","anchor":"A-plugin-can-contribute-only-vocabulary","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The rules are optional. A plugin can teach the parser a word and leave the behavior to the host, which handles the shared intent in its own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension Intent {","    #verb(\"appraise\", [\"appraise\", .directObject])","}","","struct Appraiser: GamePlugin {","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] {","        .appraise","    }","}","","\/\/ in the host:","var rules: Rules {","    gem.before(.appraise) {","        try reply(\"The \\(gem.name) is worth \\(gem[.price] ?? 0) coins.\")","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"The one thing the host doesn’t splice","anchor":"The-one-thing-the-host-doesnt-splice","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin\/statusFields"},{"type":"text","text":" adds "},{"code":"name=value","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" pairs to the play-test status footer, and it is the single member the host gets by "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"storing","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the plugin rather than by splicing it into a block of its own:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct Barometer: GamePlugin {","    var statusFields: [(String, String)] { [(\"glass\", \"falling\")] }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything else here changes what the game does, so the host opts in by hand. A status field annotates a transcript the host already asked for and changes nothing about the world — and there is no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Game"},{"type":"text","text":" block to splice it into — so the bootstrap reads it off the host’s stored properties, the same walk that catches an unlisted bundle. A plugin the host stores is found; one constructed inline inside a computed property is not."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The field is read inside a live turn frame that is then discarded, so it must be read-only — and it is sampled at the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"close","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" of the turn rather than after the turn’s counter advanced, so a field derived from "},{"code":"moves","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" names the turn it is printed under. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles#A-bundle-can-add-a-field-to-the-status-footer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the full contract, sampling point included, which is identical for both protocols."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Content-bearing plugins own their region","anchor":"Content-bearing-plugins-own-their-region","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A logic-only ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" declares no world of its own — it operates entirely over entities the host passes it. A plugin that needs to ship its ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"own","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" rooms, items, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" state is a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","type":"reference"},{"text":" instead: a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","type":"reference"},{"text":" carries ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verbs"},{"text":", and the bootstrap discovers its entities by reflection, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles#EntityIDs-are-namespaced-by-the-bundle","overridingTitle":"namespacing","isActive":true,"type":"reference","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"namespacing"}]},{"type":"text","text":" them under the bundle so a reusable plugin can’t collide with the host. List it in the game’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"content"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The two roles compose in one type. A single struct can conform to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent"},{"type":"text","text":" (for its auto-namespaced region and self-contained rules) "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" expose host-facing rule factories exactly like a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" — factories are just methods returning "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules"},{"type":"text","text":", so any type can offer them:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension Intent {","    #verb(\"donate\", [\"donate\", .directObject])","}","","struct ShrineContent: GameContent {","    let shrine = Location { name(\"Stone Shrine\"); description(\"…\") }   \/\/ its own room","    @Global var visits = 0                                             \/\/ its own state","","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] { .donate }","    var rules: Rules { shrine.onEnter { visits += 1; try reply(\"…\") } }  \/\/ self-contained","","    \/\/ Host-facing factory over a host item + host global — the GamePlugin pattern.","    func offering(of item: Item,","                  merit: @escaping @Sendable () -> Int,","                  credit: @escaping @Sendable (Int) -> Void) -> Rules {","        item.before(.donate) { credit(item[.value] ?? 0)","            try reply(\"Your merit rises to \\(merit()).\") }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host lists it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"content"},{"type":"text","text":" (registering the namespaced region) "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" splices the factory into its own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"type":"text","text":", wiring it to host declarations:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct PilgrimGame: Game {","    let shrineKit = ShrineContent()","    @Global var merit = 0","    let coin = Item { name(\"brass coin\"); trait(.value, 7) }","","    var content: GameContents { shrineKit }","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] { shrineKit.verbs }","    var rules: Rules {","        shrineKit.offering(of: coin, merit: { merit }, credit: { merit += $0 })","    }","    \/\/ map: place coin in shrineKit.shrine, wire plaza ↔ shrineKit.shrine, …","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"References stay token-based across the boundary, so a host item can sit in a plugin room and a plugin rule can hook a host entity regardless of the namespace."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-first-party-plugins","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The first-party plugins"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Seven shipped library products exercise both plugin shapes for real — each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"imports only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gnusto"},{"type":"text","text":", and the Zork 1 executable target is the worked"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example that wires the first four:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Product"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shape"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Owns"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host passes"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoDangerousDark","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one dark-turn counter, the grue daemon"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"prose + grace period at init; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"suspended"},{"text":" to make the dark harmless for a stretch (never ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stopDaemon(\"grue\")"},{"text":", which freezes the count)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoScoring","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"award-once registers","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the award table to ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(awards:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", treasures + the trophy case to ","type":"text"},{"code":"treasures(_:into:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoActors","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GamePlugin","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"nothing — position ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"is"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the actor’s placement","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"actors, room sets, candidates to ","type":"text"},{"code":"roams","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"steals","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"reaction","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoMeleeCombat","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"the combat ledger (health\/stun\/engagement by key)","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"villains, weapons, prose to "},{"code":"villain","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"aggression","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and each villain’s "},{"code":"strikesFirst","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" odds of picking a fight nobody offered him"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoSpellcasting"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the spell memory and the energy pool"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"spells + their "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SpellCost"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spell(_:cost:effect:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoClock"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the clock’s offset and pause state"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"start time, minutes per turn, alarms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"at(_:named:perform:)"},{"type":"text","text":", timetables to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"schedule(_:daemonName:_:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoConversation"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the facts the player has worked out, and which answers each actor has already given"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"actors + topic rows to "},{"code":"topics(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"again:"},{"type":"text","text":" lines for the answers that should land once), opening lines to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greeting(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", evidence to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shows(_:to:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The split follows one rule: a system that needs its own saved state is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" bundle (its ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s namespace automatically and travel in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"saves); a stateless toolkit is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"GamePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Plugin prose arrives as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"init and factory parameters","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" with sensible defaults — ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fixed struct, so a plugin can’t add lines to it retroactively; what it can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"do is take its lines from the host, which also keeps every player-visible"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"string in the game’s own voice."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Worked examples","anchor":"Worked-examples"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Sources\/Lighthouse\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a small host that splices just two: ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoScoring","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (a ","type":"text"},{"code":"visit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" award and a one-off ","type":"text"},{"code":"awardOnce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", both declared in its award table so the bootstrap can check ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxScore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoActors","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (a roaming keeper). The smallest of these examples.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Sources\/Zork1\/Zork1.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the host that wires four first-party plugins over entities from three content bundles.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Sources\/Gramarye\/Gramarye.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a small original game built entirely around ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoSpellcasting","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with one puzzle per casting paradigm.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Fulminate\/Fulminate.swift"},{"text":" — the mystery demo, built around ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoClock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": an evening on a wall clock with three alarms bracketing it. Its story and mechanics contract live in ","type":"text"},{"code":"docs\/games\/fulminate.md","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Sources\/KindlyDeep\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a survival-and-companion host: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeV